     These functions retrieve the ELF header from the ELF descriptor _e_l_f, al‐
     locating a new header if needed.  File data structures are translated to
     their in-memory representations as described in elf(3).

     Function eellff3322__nneewweehhddrr() returns a pointer to a 32 bit _E_l_f_3_2___E_h_d_r struc‐
     ture.  Function eellff6644__nneewweehhddrr() returns a pointer to a 64 bit _E_l_f_6_4___E_h_d_r
     structure.

     When argument _e_l_f_c_l_a_s_s has value ELFCLASS32, function ggeellff__nneewweehhddrr() re‐
     turns the value returned by eellff3322__nneewweehhddrr(_e_l_f).  When argument _e_l_f_c_l_a_s_s
     has value ELFCLASS64 it returns the value returned by eellff6644__nneewweehhddrr(_e_l_f).

     If a fresh header structure is allocated, the members of the structure
     are initialized as follows:

